Python Housing Price Prediction Project (Brief Introduction)

This project focuses on predicting house prices using Python and Linear Regression, a supervised machine learning algorithm. The objective is to analyze various housing features and estimate property prices based on historical data. The project includes data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis (EDA), visualization using charts and graphs, model training, and performance evaluation.

Columns Used

Typical housing dataset columns include:

Column	Description
Area	Total area of the house (sq. ft.)
Bedrooms	Number of bedrooms
Bathrooms	Number of bathrooms
Stories	Number of floors
Parking	Available parking spaces
Main Road	Whether the house is connected to a main road
Guest Room	Availability of a guest room
Basement	Presence of a basement
Hot Water Heating	Hot water heating facility
Air Conditioning	Availability of AC
Furnishing Status	Furnished, Semi-furnished, or Unfurnished
Price	Target variable (House Price)
Visualizations Used

The project utilizes several charts to understand the data and identify relationships between features and house prices:

Histogram – Distribution of house prices and area.
Scatter Plot – Relationship between area and price.
Bar Chart – Comparison of average prices across furnishing statuses.
Correlation Heatmap – Shows correlation between numerical features.
Box Plot – Detects outliers in price and area data.

